  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Asthma through a chain of indications that link it to the condition. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone may be associated with Asthma via indirect pathways, primarily through the use of Hydrocortisone Acetate and Methylprednisolone. These corticosteroids are indicated for conditions that can lead to Asthma, such as Erythema Multiforme and Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, which are themselves linked to Asthma in the provided evidence. The presence of these indirect pathways implies a possible role of Prednisolone in the development or exacerbation of Asthma, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these indications highlights a potential dependency on corticosteroids in the management of Asthma, suggesting a broader pharmacological relationship that warrants further investigation.",
